  "worked_solution": "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=\u27e85,2,3\u27e9.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\u27e83,1,-4\u27e9+t\u27e85,2,3\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83+5t,1+2t,-4+3t\u27e9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e83+5t,1+2t,-4+3t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e8-3,2,-1\u27e9 & =39 \\\\ \u27e83+5t,1+2t,-4+3t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-3,2,-1\u27e9 & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e83+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-12,-5,-13\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$",
